BT /F2 16.0 Tf 72.00 720.00 Td (KANDLE: Grid-Adaptive Kolmogorov-Arnold Networks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 694.00 Td (Ilse Vermeer, Rohan Kapoor, Yuki Sato \(Meridian Mathematics Group\)) Tj ET
BT /F2 12.0 Tf 72.00 664.00 Td (Abstract) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 644.00 Td (Kolmogorov-Arnold networks \(KANs\) replace the fixed activation functions of a multilayer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 631.00 Td (perceptron with learnable univariate functions. We present KANDLE, a KAN whose B-spline) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 618.00 Td (activations refine their grids during training. On the Feynman equations benchmark KANDLE) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 605.00 Td (reaches a median RMSE of 1.2e-4 with ten times fewer parameters than an MLP of similar) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 592.00 Td (accuracy.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12.0 Tf 72.00 572.00 Td (1 Introduction) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 552.00 Td (KANs are based on the Kolmogorov-Arnold representation theorem, which states that every) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 539.00 Td (continuous multivariate function on a bounded domain can be written as a finite composition) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 526.00 Td (of continuous functions of one variable and addition. A KAN layer generalises this) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 513.00 Td (construction to arbitrary widths and depths.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 493.00 Td (In a multilayer perceptron the nodes apply fixed nonlinearities and the edges carry scalar) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 480.00 Td (weights. In a KAN the learnable activation functions sit on edges and the nodes only sum) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 467.00 Td (their inputs, so every edge is a small function that can be plotted and, often, recognised.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12.0 Tf 72.00 447.00 Td (2 Method) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 427.00 Td (Each edge function is a cubic B-spline plus a residual SiLU term. The spline has order k = 3) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 414.00 Td (and G grid intervals over the range of its input:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 150.00 394.00 Td (phi\(x\) = w_b silu\(x\) + w_s sum_i c_i B_i\(x\)                     \(1\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 372.00 Td (Coarse grids train quickly but limit accuracy, and fine grids from the start train slowly.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 359.00 Td (KANDLE uses grid extension from G = 5 to G = 20 in three stages: when the loss plateaus,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 346.00 Td (each spline is refitted by least squares on a finer grid, so training continues from the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 333.00 Td (coarse solution instead of restarting.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 313.00 Td (After training, edges whose L1 norm falls below a threshold are pruned, and the remaining) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 300.00 Td (edge functions can be matched against a library of symbolic forms such as sin, exp and x^2.) Tj ET
